Gravity Grind
by Anwar Bakhos

A 2D ball-rolling time-trial game made in Unity 6 (6000.5.9f1). Two modes: **Tabletop** (tilt the board with the mouse) and **Side View** (roll and jump). Race your best-time ghost, earn medals, and build your own courses in the level editor.

## Where things are
| Folder / file | What's in it |
|---|---|
| `Assets/Scripts/` | **All the game code** (start with `Game.cs`) |
| `Assets/Resources/` | Art, sounds and font (Kenney CC0 packs + a few made for this game) |
| `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity` | The one scene the game runs in |
| `CustomLevels/` | Levels I made with the in-game editor |
| `CHANGES.txt` | Changes from my design doc |
| `CREDITS.txt` | Where the art, sounds and font came from |
| `AI_NOTES.txt` | How AI was used |
| `Packages/`, `ProjectSettings/` | Unity's own settings (needed to open the project) |

## How to play
Open the folder in Unity Hub, open `Assets/Scenes/SampleScene`, press Play.
- Tabletop: move the mouse to tilt. Side view: A/D to roll, Space to jump.
- R restarts, Esc pauses.
```
